{"questions": [{"id": "mi-1.1-01", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.1", "difficulty": "easy", "stem": "Maya can spend Sunday studying for an exam or working a shift that pays $60. She decides to study. Which of the following is her opportunity cost?", "choices": ["The $60 she could have earned", "The grade she earns on the exam", "The cost of her textbooks", "The hours she spends studying", "Nothing, because studying is free"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Opportunity cost is the value of the next-best alternative given up. By studying, Maya gives up the $60 from the shift.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.1-02", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.1", "difficulty": "medium", "stem": "A country can produce either 40 tons of wheat or 20 bolts of cloth with all of its resources, and its production possibilities curve is a straight line. What is the opportunity cost of producing one bolt of cloth?", "choices": ["0.5 ton of wheat", "20 tons of wheat", "40 tons of wheat", "2 tons of wheat", "It rises as more cloth is produced"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "Giving up 40 tons of wheat yields 20 bolts of cloth, so each bolt costs 40/20 = 2 tons. A straight-line curve means that cost is constant.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.1-03", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.1", "difficulty": "medium", "stem": "The table shows the maximum number of shirts or hats that Ana and Ben can each produce with equivalent resources. Which of the following is true?", "choices": ["Ana has a comparative advantage in shirts, and Ben has a comparative advantage in hats.", "Ana has a comparative advantage in hats.", "Ben has a comparative advantage in shirts.", "Ana has an absolute advantage in both goods.", "No mutually beneficial trade is possible."], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Ana's opportunity cost of a hat is 30/10 = 3 shirts; Ben's is 20/20 = 1 shirt. Ben is the low-cost hat producer, so Ana has the comparative advantage in shirts.", "image": "data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A//www.w3.org/2000/svg%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%20235%20108%27%20width%3D%27235%27%20height%3D%27108%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%27235%27%20height%3D%27108%27%20fill%3D%27%23fff%27/%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2710%27%20y1%3D%2712%27%20x2%3D%27225%27%20y2%3D%2712%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271.4%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2745.0%27%20y%3D%2731%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27117.5%27%20y%3D%2731%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EShirts%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27190.0%27%20y%3D%2731%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EHats%3C/text%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2710%27%20y1%3D%2740%27%20x2%3D%27225%27%20y2%3D%2740%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%27.9%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2745.0%27%20y%3D%2759%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EAna%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27117.5%27%20y%3D%2759%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E30%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27190.0%27%20y%3D%2759%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E10%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2745.0%27%20y%3D%2787%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EBen%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27117.5%27%20y%3D%2787%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E20%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27190.0%27%20y%3D%2787%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E20%3C/text%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2710%27%20y1%3D%2796%27%20x2%3D%27225%27%20y2%3D%2796%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271.4%27/%3E%3C/svg%3E"}, {"id": "mi-1.1-04", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.1", "difficulty": "hard", "stem": "Using the same table of Ana's and Ben's production, which of the following terms of trade for one hat would make both Ana and Ben better off?", "choices": ["0.5 shirt", "1 shirt", "2 shirts", "3 shirts", "4 shirts"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "Ben gives up 1 shirt to make a hat and Ana gives up 3. Any price strictly between 1 and 3 shirts per hat benefits both, so 2 shirts works.", "image": "data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A//www.w3.org/2000/svg%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%20235%20108%27%20width%3D%27235%27%20height%3D%27108%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%27235%27%20height%3D%27108%27%20fill%3D%27%23fff%27/%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2710%27%20y1%3D%2712%27%20x2%3D%27225%27%20y2%3D%2712%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271.4%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2745.0%27%20y%3D%2731%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27117.5%27%20y%3D%2731%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EShirts%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27190.0%27%20y%3D%2731%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EHats%3C/text%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2710%27%20y1%3D%2740%27%20x2%3D%27225%27%20y2%3D%2740%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%27.9%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2745.0%27%20y%3D%2759%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EAna%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27117.5%27%20y%3D%2759%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E30%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27190.0%27%20y%3D%2759%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E10%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2745.0%27%20y%3D%2787%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EBen%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27117.5%27%20y%3D%2787%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E20%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27190.0%27%20y%3D%2787%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E20%3C/text%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2710%27%20y1%3D%2796%27%20x2%3D%27225%27%20y2%3D%2796%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271.4%27/%3E%3C/svg%3E"}, {"id": "mi-1.1-05", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.1", "difficulty": "easy", "stem": "Tennis rackets are a normal good. Which of the following will increase the demand for tennis rackets?", "choices": ["A decrease in the price of tennis rackets", "An increase in the price of tennis balls, a complement", "A decrease in the price of badminton rackets, a substitute", "An improvement in racket production technology", "An increase in consumers' incomes"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "Higher income raises demand for a normal good. A change in the racket's own price is a movement along demand, and a technology change affects supply.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.1-06", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.1", "difficulty": "medium", "stem": "The price of coffee beans, an input for coffee shops, falls at the same time that a widely publicized study reports health benefits from drinking coffee. What happens to the equilibrium price and quantity of coffee?", "choices": ["Price increases and quantity increases.", "Price decreases and quantity decreases.", "Price increases and quantity is indeterminate.", "Price is indeterminate and quantity decreases.", "Price is indeterminate and quantity increases."], "answer": 4, "explanation": "Cheaper beans shift supply right and the study shifts demand right. Both raise quantity, but they push price in opposite directions, so the price change is indeterminate.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.1-07", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.1", "difficulty": "medium", "stem": "The graph shows the market for a good. If the price is $8, which of the following exists in the market?", "choices": ["A shortage of 20 units", "A surplus of 50 units", "A shortage of 30 units", "A surplus of 20 units", "The market is in equilibrium"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "At $8, quantity demanded is 30 and quantity supplied is 50. Supply exceeds demand by 20 units, which is a surplus.", "image": "data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A//www.w3.org/2000/svg%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%20460%20330%27%20width%3D%27460%27%20height%3D%27330%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%27460%27%20height%3D%27330%27%20fill%3D%27%23fff%27/%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2772%27%20y1%3D%27276%27%20x2%3D%2772%27%20y2%3D%2716%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271.4%27/%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2772%27%20y1%3D%27276%27%20x2%3D%27438%27%20y2%3D%27276%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271.4%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%276%27%20y%3D%2713%27%20font-size%3D%2713%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EPrice%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27440%27%20y%3D%27316%27%20text-anchor%3D%27end%27%20font-size%3D%2713%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EQuantity%3C/text%3E%3Cpolyline%20points%3D%2772.0%2C109.3%20274.5%2C109.3%27%20fill%3D%27none%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271%27%20stroke-dasharray%3D%275%204%27/%3E%3Cpolyline%20points%3D%27193.5%2C109.3%20193.5%2C276.0%27%20fill%3D%27none%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271%27%20stroke-dasharray%3D%275%204%27/%3E%3Cpolyline%20points%3D%27274.5%2C109.3%20274.5%2C276.0%27%20fill%3D%27none%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271%27%20stroke-dasharray%3D%275%204%27/%3E%3Cpolyline%20points%3D%2772.0%2C151.0%20234.0%2C151.0%27%20fill%3D%27none%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271%27%20stroke-dasharray%3D%275%204%27/%3E%3Cpolyline%20points%3D%27234.0%2C151.0%20234.0%2C276.0%27%20fill%3D%27none%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271%27%20stroke-dasharray%3D%275%204%27/%3E%3Cpolyline%20points%3D%27112.5%2C26.0%20315.0%2C234.3%27%20fill%3D%27none%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271.8%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27321.0%27%20y%3D%27238.3%27%20font-size%3D%2713%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3ED%3C/text%3E%3Cpolyline%20points%3D%27112.5%2C276.0%20355.5%2C26.0%27%20fill%3D%27none%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271.8%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27361.5%27%20y%3D%2730.0%27%20font-size%3D%2713%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3ES%3C/text%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%27193.5%27%20y1%3D%27276%27%20x2%3D%27193.5%27%20y2%3D%27281%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27193.5%27%20y%3D%27296%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2712.5%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E30%3C/text%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%27234.0%27%20y1%3D%27276%27%20x2%3D%27234.0%27%20y2%3D%27281%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27234.0%27%20y%3D%27296%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2712.5%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E40%3C/text%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%27274.5%27%20y1%3D%27276%27%20x2%3D%27274.5%27%20y2%3D%27281%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27274.5%27%20y%3D%27296%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2712.5%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E50%3C/text%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2767%27%20y1%3D%27151.0%27%20x2%3D%2772%27%20y2%3D%27151.0%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2763%27%20y%3D%27155.0%27%20text-anchor%3D%27end%27%20font-size%3D%2712.5%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E%246%3C/text%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2767%27%20y1%3D%27109.3%27%20x2%3D%2772%27%20y2%3D%27109.3%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2763%27%20y%3D%27113.3%27%20text-anchor%3D%27end%27%20font-size%3D%2712.5%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E%248%3C/text%3E%3C/svg%3E"}, {"id": "mi-1.2-01", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.2", "difficulty": "easy", "stem": "When the price of a good rises by 10 percent, the quantity demanded falls by 25 percent. Over this range, demand is", "choices": ["perfectly inelastic", "inelastic", "unit elastic", "perfectly elastic", "elastic"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "The price elasticity is 25/10 = 2.5. A coefficient greater than 1 means demand is elastic.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.2-02", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.2", "difficulty": "medium", "stem": "A theater raises its ticket prices and finds that its total revenue falls. This means that over this price range, demand for tickets is", "choices": ["elastic", "inelastic", "unit elastic", "perfectly inelastic", "upward sloping"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "Price and total revenue moved in opposite directions, which happens only when demand is elastic. Quantity fell by a larger percentage than price rose.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.2-03", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.2", "difficulty": "medium", "stem": "The cross-price elasticity of demand between Good X and Good Y is 1.5. Goods X and Y are", "choices": ["complements", "normal goods", "inferior goods", "substitutes", "unrelated goods"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "A positive cross-price elasticity means a higher price of one good raises demand for the other, which is the definition of substitutes.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.2-04", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.2", "difficulty": "medium", "stem": "When Dilnoza's income rises by 10 percent, she buys 4 percent more bread. What is her income elasticity of demand for bread, and what type of good is bread for her?", "choices": ["2.5; a normal good", "0.4; a normal good", "−0.4; an inferior good", "0.4; an inferior good", "−2.5; an inferior good"], "answer": 1, "explanation": "Income elasticity is 4/10 = 0.4. Because it is positive, bread is a normal good for her; because it is below 1, it is a necessity.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.2-05", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.2", "difficulty": "hard", "stem": "When the price of a good rises from $4 to $6, the quantity demanded falls from 120 to 80 units. Using the midpoint method, demand over this range is", "choices": ["unit elastic", "perfectly inelastic", "inelastic", "elastic", "perfectly elastic"], "answer": 0, "explanation": "The percentage change in quantity is −40/100 = −40% and in price is 2/5 = 40%, giving an elasticity of 1. Total revenue stays at $480 in both cases, which confirms unit elasticity.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.2-06", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.2", "difficulty": "easy", "stem": "Demand for which of the following is most likely to be price inelastic?", "choices": ["A particular brand of breakfast cereal", "Restaurant meals", "Airline tickets for vacations", "Designer sneakers", "Insulin for a diabetic patient"], "answer": 4, "explanation": "Goods with few substitutes that are necessities have inelastic demand. Insulin has no close substitute for someone who needs it.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.3-01", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.3", "difficulty": "easy", "stem": "A firm decides whether to produce one more unit of output. According to marginal analysis, the firm should produce the unit if", "choices": ["its total revenue is greater than its total cost", "its average cost is falling", "it can sell every unit at the same price", "the additional benefit of the unit is at least as large as its additional cost", "its fixed cost is covered"], "answer": 3, "explanation": "Marginal analysis compares the extra benefit of one more unit with its extra cost. The unit is worth producing when marginal benefit is at least marginal cost.", "image": ""}, {"id": "mi-1.3-02", "subject": "micro", "unit": 1, "topic": "1.3", "difficulty": "medium", "stem": "The table shows Kamila's marginal benefit and marginal cost of hours of tutoring. How many hours should she buy to maximize her net benefit?", "choices": ["1 hour", "2 hours", "3 hours", "4 hours", "5 hours"], "answer": 2, "explanation": "She should buy every hour for which marginal benefit is at least marginal cost. The third hour has MB = MC = $18; the fourth has MB of $12 but MC of $22.", "image": "data:image/svg+xml;charset=utf-8,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%27http%3A//www.w3.org/2000/svg%27%20viewBox%3D%270%200%20540%20192%27%20width%3D%27540%27%20height%3D%27192%27%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%27540%27%20height%3D%27192%27%20fill%3D%27%23fff%27/%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2710%27%20y1%3D%2712%27%20x2%3D%27530%27%20y2%3D%2712%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%271.4%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2792.5%27%20y%3D%2731%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EHours%20of%20tutoring%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27270.0%27%20y%3D%2731%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EMarginal%20benefit%20%28%24%29%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27447.5%27%20y%3D%2731%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3EMarginal%20cost%20%28%24%29%3C/text%3E%3Cline%20x1%3D%2710%27%20y1%3D%2740%27%20x2%3D%27530%27%20y2%3D%2740%27%20stroke%3D%27%23000%27%20stroke-width%3D%27.9%27/%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2792.5%27%20y%3D%2759%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E1%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27270.0%27%20y%3D%2759%27%20text-anchor%3D%27middle%27%20font-size%3D%2714%27%20font-family%3D%27Georgia%2CTimes%20New%20Roman%2Cserif%27%3E30%3C/text%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%27447.5%27%20y%3